Change streams require a replica set. Testcontainers + replica-set mode:
import { MongoDBContainer } from '@testcontainers/mongodb';
// recent versions auto-enable replica set; check the version of the package
Or MongoMemoryReplSet. Then test:
test('change stream sees insert', async () => {
const cs = db.collection('events').watch();
const seen = (async () => {
for await (const ch of cs) return ch;
})();
await db.collection('events').insertOne({ x: 1 });
const change = await Promise.race([seen, sleep(2000).then(() => { throw new Error('timeout'); })]);
expect(change.operationType).toBe('insert');
await cs.close();
});
Test consumer logic similarly — feed events through your handler, assert side effects.

test('transfer rolls back on error', async () => {
await accounts.insertMany([{ _id: 'A', balance: 100 }, { _id: 'B', balance: 0 }]);
await expect(transfer('A', 'B', 200)).rejects.toThrow('insufficient');
expect((await accounts.findOne({ _id: 'A' })).balance).toBe(100);
expect((await accounts.findOne({ _id: 'B' })).balance).toBe(0);
});
Transactions require replica set — same Testcontainers / in-memory replica-set setup as change streams.
